  {
   "topic": "Gain groups",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "The suffix after BC807 is the hFE group at IC = -100 mA, VCE = -1.0 V: -16 covers 100 to 250, -25 covers 160 to 400, -40 covers 250 to 600. At IC = -500 mA every group is held only to a minimum hFE of 40. The other limits are common to all three."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Typical curves",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "Each gain group has its own typical curves (BC807-16LT1, BC807-25LT1, BC807-40LT1) of DC gain, VCE(sat), VBE(sat) and VBE(on) at -55, 25 and 150 °C, and of fT. The saturation-region, temperature-coefficient and capacitance curves are the same for all three groups, and one safe operating area covers them all."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Safe operating area",
   "page": 9,
   "text": "The thermal limit holds collector current at 0.5 A up to about 0.4 V collector to emitter and falls to about 4.5 mA at 45 V. The 1 s, 100 ms, 10 ms and 1 ms lines lie above it, each flat at about 0.8 A from 0.1 V and running down to 45 V."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Thermal derating",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Allowed dissipation falls linearly above 25 °C ambient: by 1.8 mW/°C from 225 mW on the FR board, and by 2.4 mW/°C from 300 mW on alumina."
  }
